00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,688
听：A Course That Opened a Door.

2
00:00:02,688 --> 00:00:05,376
跟读：A Course That Opened a Door.

3
00:00:05,376 --> 00:00:27,816
听：When Mei returned to college, she needed a course that would fit around her job. The college offered tuition in the evening, but enrolment was falling. Some applicants lacked childcare, while others could not afford the fees. A tutor asked Mei to help investigate the problem.

4
00:00:27,816 --> 00:00:50,256
跟读：When Mei returned to college, she needed a course that would fit around her job. The college offered tuition in the evening, but enrolment was falling. Some applicants lacked childcare, while others could not afford the fees. A tutor asked Mei to help investigate the problem.

5
00:00:50,256 --> 00:01:15,048
听：Mei interviewed several adults about their access to education. Each learner had a different timetable, and much of the advice online was confusing. There was little information about financial support. She realised that a flexible curriculum would be useful only if people could actually attend the lessons.

6
00:01:15,048 --> 00:01:39,840
跟读：Mei interviewed several adults about their access to education. Each learner had a different timetable, and much of the advice online was confusing. There was little information about financial support. She realised that a flexible curriculum would be useful only if people could actually attend the lessons.

7
00:01:39,840 --> 00:02:05,040
听：The college has introduced a small grant for eligible applicants. Since September, Mei has been helping new students complete their forms. She completed her own application last week. The new assessment includes a practical project, so students can demonstrate skills as well as remember facts.

8
